problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set of children indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$.
- Each child $$i$$ has a selection cost $$c_i$$.
- The planning horizon is a single decision period, so the decision is whether each child is included in the trip or not.
- The planning goal is to choose a subset of children that minimizes total selection cost while satisfying all family rules and trip-size limits.
- A child-selection decision is represented by:
  - $$x_i$$: a binary variable that equals $$1$$ if child $$i$$ is taken on the trip and $$0$$ otherwise.
  - The selected set is the collection of all children with $$x_i = 1$$.
  - The total trip cost is the sum of the costs of all selected children.
- Mandatory participation rules:
  - Some children may be required to be included in every feasible plan.
- Capacity rules:
  - The total number of selected children may not exceed an upper limit $$U$$.
  - The total number of selected children must be at least a lower limit $$L$$.
- Compatibility rules:
  - If one child is selected, certain other children must not be selected together with that child.
- Precedence or dependency rules:
  - If one child is selected, one or more other children must also be selected.
- The objective is to minimize the total cost of the selected children subject to the mandatory, capacity, compatibility, and dependency rules.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_i$$ for each $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$, indicating whether each child is selected.
  - The resulting selected subset of children.
  - The total minimized trip cost.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "$$\\mathcal{I}$$": {
      "description": "Set of children indexed by $$i$$.",
      "size": "$$n$$"
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "$$c_i$$": {
      "description": "Selection cost of child $$i$$.",
      "shape": ["$$n$$"]
    },
    "$$U$$": {
      "description": "Maximum number of children that may be selected.",
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "$$L$$": {
      "description": "Minimum number of children that must be selected.",
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "$$\\mathcal{M}$$": {
      "description": "Set of mandatory children that must be selected.",
      "type": "set of indices"
    },
    "$$\\mathcal{P}$$": {
      "description": "Set of ordered dependency rules where selecting one child requires selecting another child or group of children.",
      "type": "list of rules"
    },
    "$$\\mathcal{Q}$$": {
      "description": "Set of incompatibility rules where selecting one child forbids selecting another child or group of children together.",
      "type": "list of rules"
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "decision_variables": {
    "$$x_i$$": {
      "description": "Binary selection variable for child $$i$$.",
      "shape": ["$$n$$"],
      "values": ["$$0$$", "$$1$$"]
    }
  },
  "selected_children": {
    "description": "The set of children with $$x_i = 1$$.",
    "type": "list of indices"
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "description": "The minimized total selection cost of the chosen children.",
    "type": "number"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "sets": {
    "$$\\mathcal{I}$$": {
      "description": "Children",
      "elements": ["$$\\text{Harry}$$", "$$\\text{Hermione}$$", "$$\\text{Ron}$$", "$$\\text{Fred}$$", "$$\\text{George}$$", "$$\\text{Ginny}$$"],
      "size": "$$6$$"
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "$$c_i$$": {
      "$$\\text{Harry}$$": "$$1200$$",
      "$$\\text{Hermione}$$": "$$1650$$",
      "$$\\text{Ron}$$": "$$750$$",
      "$$\\text{Fred}$$": "$$800$$",
      "$$\\text{George}$$": "$$800$$",
      "$$\\text{Ginny}$$": "$$1500$$"
    },
    "$$U$$": "$$4$$",
    "$$L$$": "$$3$$",
    "$$\\mathcal{M}$$": ["$$\\text{Ginny}$$"],
    "$$\\mathcal{P}$$": [
      {
        "if": "$$\\text{George}$$",
        "then": ["$$\\text{Fred}$$", "$$\\text{Hermione}$$"]
      }
    ],
    "$$\\mathcal{Q}$$": [
      {
        "if": "$$\\text{Harry}$$",
        "forbid": ["$$\\text{Fred}$$", "$$\\text{George}$$"]
      }
    ]
  }
}
